sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant PO as ODH/RHOAI Platform Operator
    participant User as User / GitOps
    participant K8s as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant Mod as ogx-module manager
    participant WH as Webhook Service<br/>443→9443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Op as OGX Operator
    participant Reg as Container Registry<br/>443/TCP (80 fallback)
    participant OGX as OGX Server Service<br/>8321/TCP HTTP
    participant Praxis as Praxis Gateway
    participant Ingr as Ingress Controller<br/>443/TCP edge TLS
    participant Back as Providers / SQL / KV

    Note over PO,Op: Flow 1 - Module install of the OGX operator
    PO->>K8s: Create OGX CR default-ogx + module ConfigMap<br/>SA token
    Mod->>K8s: Watch OGX CR, ConfigMap<br/>SA token
    Mod->>K8s: Apply rendered root operator CRD, RBAC,<br/>Deployment, webhook, ServiceMonitor
    Mod->>K8s: Read Deployment readiness, webhook Secrets,<br/>OGXServer conditions
    Mod->>K8s: Update OGX status

    Note over User,OGX: Flow 2 - OGXServer reconciliation
    User->>K8s: Create OGXServer<br/>User token
    K8s->>WH: AdmissionReview (CREATE/UPDATE)<br/>TLS cluster profile, service-CA
    WH-->>K8s: Allowed / Denied (+ Praxis warnings)
    K8s-->>Op: Watch event OGXServer
    Op->>Reg: GET /v2/.../manifests, config blob<br/>Anonymous, HTTPS then HTTP fallback
    Reg-->>Op: OCI config labels (base config)
    Op->>K8s: Create ConfigMap name-config-hash, Deployment,<br/>Service, NetworkPolicy, PVC, HPA, PDB, Ingress, RoleBinding
    Op->>OGX: GET /v1/providers, /v1/version<br/>plain HTTP, no auth, 5s timeout
    OGX-->>Op: Providers + version
    Op->>K8s: Update OGXServer status

    Note over Praxis,Back: Flow 3 - Client traffic in Praxis mode
    Praxis->>OGX: API request (from end user via 443/TCP HTTPS)<br/>x-user-id / x-tenant-id headers
    OGX->>Back: Provider-specific HTTPS/TCP<br/>Secret-injected credentials, CA bundle
    Back-->>OGX: Response
    OGX-->>Praxis: Response

    Note over Ingr,OGX: Flow 4 - Legacy external-access mode
    Ingr->>OGX: Forward from external client (TLS terminated at edge)<br/>plain HTTP, distribution-defined auth
    OGX-->>Ingr: Response
